   "about": {
    "text": [
     "Plebiscites held in Limerick City and County Council, Waterford City and County Council and Cork City Council on whether each local authority should have a directly elected mayor. The plebiscites in Waterford and Cork City were rejected with 49.2% Yes / 50.8% No and 49.3% Yes / 50.7% No votes respectively, but the plebiscite in Limerick was passed with a 52.4% Yes / 47.6% No vote."
    ],
